---
import Base from '../../../quran/layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Privacy" description="How the Quran Library handles your data." open>
  <div class="narrow" style="padding-top:36px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px;max-width:760px">
    <h1 style="margin:0">Privacy</h1>
    <p style="margin:0">Last updated: 12 November 2026.</p>
    <h2 style="margin:8px 0 0;font-size:20px">Your account</h2>
    <p style="margin:0">To use the Quran Library you create an account with your name, whether you are a brother or a sister (so the Sheikh addresses you properly), a username and a password. These are kept by Al-Huda Islamic Centre in a Google Sheet that only the centre's administrators can open. Your password is never stored: only a salted hash of it, which cannot be turned back into the password.</p>
    <p style="margin:0">So that they follow you to another computer or phone, your bookmarks, your last reading place, your Recite and Hifz test set-ups and your reading settings are saved to your account. When you finish a Hifz test, its result (the passage, how many words were right first time, prompts and hints, the grade and the words to revise) is added to your record. Signing out removes them from the device you are using.</p>
    <p style="margin:0">We have no analytics, and we do not sell or share your data. To have your account and records deleted, ask the centre.</p>
    <h2 style="margin:8px 0 0;font-size:20px">Microphone and speech</h2>
    <p style="margin:0">Recite and the Hifz test use the microphone only while you have pressed the microphone button. Your voice is turned into text by your device’s speech service: Google on Android and in Chrome, Apple on iPhone and in Safari. That service may process the audio on their servers under their own privacy policies. The app receives only the text, uses it to follow your recitation, and does not record or store audio.</p>
    <h2 style="margin:8px 0 0;font-size:20px">Content from other services</h2>
    <p style="margin:0">Recitation audio streams from EveryAyah, and fonts may load from Google Fonts. These services see a normal web request from your device, as with any website.</p>
    <h2 style="margin:8px 0 0;font-size:20px">Contact</h2>
    <p style="margin:0">Questions, or to delete your account: ask Al-Huda Islamic Centre.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
